      "side": 1,
      "message": "In this CL, we introduced a speed feature `adaptive_luma_filter_skip` for low-complexity decode mode. Initially, this sf is tested with resetting chroma filter levels as well. However, the speed up observed is not much as compared with the BD-Rate loss. Hence, to minimize BD-rate drop, this logic is limited to luma only.\n\nThe visual quality tests showed blocking artifacts for ‘blue_sky_480p25’ at cpu_used\u003d1, --target-bitrate\u003d75 kbps in both the reference and modified versions. For this configuration, an unexpected vertical line was observed in the reference version but the same was not seen after this change. However, the modified version has slightly more artifacts at the boundaries of the video frame.\n\nPerformance results of encoder and decoder for the streams generated\nwith low complexity decode enabled.\n\n```\n                        Instruction Count                                               \n                          Reduction(%)                BD-Rate Loss(%)                 Time Reduction(%)\ncpu-used  Resolution    Encoder   Decoder    avg.psnr    ssim       vmaf     vmaf_neg  dav1d Decoder \n   1        LOWRES2     -0.031    4.013      0.0212    0.0170    -0.0793    -0.0721      3.457\n   1        MIDRES2     -0.052    3.832      0.0541    0.0240     0.0121    -0.0002      3.137\n   1     SHORTS608P     -0.027    4.123      0.1369    0.1277     0.0064    -0.0033      3.472\n   1         HDRES2      0.068    2.935      0.0313    0.0055     0.0057    -0.0015      2.539\n   1        Average     -0.011    3.745      0.0645    0.0476    -0.0128    -0.0185      3.166\n                                                                                         \n   2        LOWRES2     -0.021    4.100      0.0201   -0.0610    -0.0874    -0.1099      2.827\n   2        MIDRES2      0.008    3.990      0.0416    0.0000    -0.0838    -0.0518      3.271\n   2     SHORTS608P     -0.001    4.201      0.2187    0.1683    -0.0176    -0.